{
  "number": 9,
  "chapter": "Romans 9",
  "source": "https://berean.bible/downloads.htm",
  "translation": "Berean Standard Bible (BSB)",
  "verses": [
    {
      "verse": 1,
      "text": "I speak the truth in Christ; I am not lying, as confirmed by my conscience in the Holy Spirit."
    },
    {
      "verse": 2,
      "text": "I have deep sorrow and unceasing anguish in my heart."
    },
    {
      "verse": 3,
      "text": "For I could wish that I myself were cursed and cut off from Christ for the sake of my brothers, my own flesh and blood,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 4,
      "text": "the people of Israel. Theirs is the adoption as sons; theirs the divine glory and the covenants; theirs the giving of the law, the temple worship, and the promises."
    },
    {
      "verse": 5,
      "text": "Theirs are the patriarchs, and from them proceeds the human descent of Christ, who is God over all, forever worthy of praise! Amen."
    },
    {
      "verse": 6,
      "text": "It is not as though God’s word has failed. For not all who are descended from Israel are Israel."
    },
    {
      "verse": 7,
      "text": "Nor because they are Abraham’s descendants are they all his children. On the contrary, “Through Isaac your offspring will be reckoned.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 8,
      "text": "So it is not the children of the flesh who are God’s children, but it is the children of the promise who are regarded as offspring."
    },
    {
      "verse": 9,
      "text": "For this is what the promise stated: “At the appointed time I will return, and Sarah will have a son.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 10,
      "text": "Not only that, but Rebecca’s children were conceived by one man, our father Isaac."
    },
    {
      "verse": 11,
      "text": "Yet before the twins were born or had done anything good or bad, in order that God’s plan of election might stand,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 12,
      "text": "not by works but by Him who calls, she was told, “The older will serve the younger.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 13,
      "text": "So it is written: “Jacob I loved, but Esau I hated.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 14,
      "text": "What then shall we say? Is God unjust? Certainly not!"
    },
    {
      "verse": 15,
      "text": "For He says to Moses: “I will have mercy on whom I have mercy, and I will have compassion on whom I have compassion.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 16,
      "text": "So then, it does not depend on man’s desire or effort, but on God’s mercy."
    },
    {
      "verse": 17,
      "text": "For the Scripture says to Pharaoh: “I raised you up for this very purpose, that I might display My power in you, and that My name might be proclaimed in all the earth.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 18,
      "text": "Therefore God has mercy on whom He wants to have mercy, and He hardens whom He wants to harden."
    },
    {
      "verse": 19,
      "text": "One of you will say to me, “Then why does God still find fault? For who can resist His will?”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 20,
      "text": "But who are you, O man, to talk back to God? Shall what is formed say to Him who formed it, “Why did You make me like this?”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 21,
      "text": "Does not the potter have the right to make from the same lump of clay one vessel for special occasions and another for common use?"
    },
    {
      "verse": 22,
      "text": "What if God, intending to show His wrath and make His power known, bore with great patience the vessels of His wrath, prepared for destruction?"
    },
    {
      "verse": 23,
      "text": "What if He did this to make the riches of His glory known to the vessels of His mercy, whom He prepared in advance for glory —"
    },
    {
      "verse": 24,
      "text": "including us, whom He has called not only from the Jews, but also from the Gentiles?"
    },
    {
      "verse": 25,
      "text": "As He says in Hosea: “I will call them ‘My People’ who are not My people, and I will call her ‘My Beloved’ who is not My beloved,”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 26,
      "text": "and, “It will happen that in the very place where it was said to them, ‘You are not My people,’ they will be called ‘sons of the living God.’”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 27,
      "text": "Isaiah cries out concerning Israel: “Though the number of the Israelites is like the sand of the sea, only the remnant will be saved."
    },
    {
      "verse": 28,
      "text": "For the Lord will carry out His sentence on the earth thoroughly and decisively.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 29,
      "text": "It is just as Isaiah foretold: “Unless the Lord of Hosts had left us descendants, we would have become like Sodom, we would have resembled Gomorrah.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 30,
      "text": "What then will we say? That the Gentiles, who did not pursue righteousness, have obtained it, a righteousness that is by faith;"
    },
    {
      "verse": 31,
      "text": "but Israel, who pursued a law of righteousness, has not attained it."
    },
    {
      "verse": 32,
      "text": "Why not? Because their pursuit was not by faith, but as if it were by works. They stumbled over the stumbling stone,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 33,
      "text": "as it is written: “See, I lay in Zion a stone of stumbling and a rock of offense; and the one who believes in Him will never be put to shame.”"
    }
  ],
